    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d88131a5",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: this_one_time_at_camp; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two workers in hard hats at an industrial site, with text overlay reading 'this one time at camp' and 'someone had too much gas.' The scene is juxtaposed with the text to create a humorous, albeit crude, joke implying a worker experienced a gas-related mishap. While the humor is based on a mundane workplace incident, the phrase 'too much gas' is a vulgar euphemism for flatulence, which can be considered offensive or crude. The meme's intent is to elicit laughter through shock value and taboo humor, but it lacks any direct targeting of specific protected groups. The humor is not inherently hateful or abusive, but it may be deemed inappropriate or offensive by some audiences due to its crude nature. The overall intent is to entertain through vulgar, workplace-related humor, which may be considered harmful or offensive due to its crude content, even if it does not target any specific group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_06f27293"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
